Content follows widely shared Shaiva tradition: the churning of the ocean (Samudra Manthan) and the Halahala poison held in
Shiva's throat (Neelakantha); Mount Kailash; Adiyogi; Nataraja. The Pancha Bhuta Sthalam: earth, Ekambareswarar Temple,
Kanchipuram; water, Jambukeswarar Temple, Thiruvanaikaval; fire, Arunachaleswarar Temple, Tiruvannamalai (the Karthigai Deepam
lit on Arunachala hill); air, Srikalahasteeswara Temple, Srikalahasti (the lamp said to flicker without wind); space, Thillai
Nataraja Temple, Chidambaram (the Chidambara Rahasyam). The Panchakshara Na-ma-shi-va-ya with one syllable per element, as
commonly given. The temples, lamp, curtain and landscapes are painted from imagination, not drawn from the real sites.
Everything else (score, foley, paper, all painting) is original and generated in code for this film.
Rendering and tools: the Lemo-Opuscar style library (Watercolor Brush style) and its core/ tools.
